From: "D.R.racer" <drracer@seznam.cz>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 13:31:34 +0200
Subject: drm/sun4i: tv: add VGA output for A10/A20

The A10/A20 TV encoders can drive a VGA connector: in "VGA mode" three
DACs output R, G and B taken straight from the display backend, and
the TCON channel 1 provides HSYNC and VSYNC. The Cubietruck has its
VGA connector wired this way, and the vendor 3.4 kernel uses it as its
default output.

When the TV encoder's output port is linked to a "vga-connector" node,
register a DAC encoder and a VGA connector instead of the composite one.
The connector reads EDID and detects the monitor over the DDC bus given
by the connector's ddc-i2c-bus property, and falls back to the standard
modes within the 150 MHz limit (up to 1920x1080) when the monitor gives
no EDID. A monitor that does not answer on DDC is reported with an
unknown status rather than as disconnected, as display-connector does
for VGA: some cables, adapters and switches do not wire the DDC pins.
Polling therefore only notices a monitor being attached; an unplugged or
swapped monitor shows up at the next probe that userspace requests.
Without a DDC bus it leaves the modes to the probe helper, which applies
an EDID override when the connector is forced on and otherwise adds the
modes up to 1024x768. The I2C adapter is looked up when first needed
rather than at probe or bind time, so the display pipeline never waits
for an I2C controller; if the controller is not there yet at the first
probe, that probe gets the fallback modes and polling picks up the
monitor later.

The register values are those of the vendor driver (TVE_set_vga_mode),
checked against a Cubietruck running it. The backend keeps its RGB
output (no RGB to YUV conversion as for composite). Modes are limited
to 150 MHz, which covers the vendor driver's VGA modes up to 1680x1050
(146.25 MHz) and 1920x1080 at 60 Hz (148.5 MHz).

Only the A10 compatible (A10 and A20) gets the VGA case; the H3 and H5
encoders stay composite-only. Only tested on A20.

Also stop the graph walk at VGA connectors: sun4i_drv would otherwise
add the connector node as a component that never binds. And double the
walk's queue to 32 nodes: with TV encoder endpoints on both A20 TCONs it
fills all 16 entries, and kfifo_put() drops nodes silently when full,
which would leave the display master waiting for a lost component.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
